<title>KYRGYZSTAN: Kyrgyz Feb inflation 2.2 pct vs 3.4 pct in Jan.</title>
<headline>Kyrgyz Feb inflation 2.2 pct vs 3.4 pct in Jan.</headline>
<dateline>BISHKEK 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kyrgyz consumer prices rose 2.2 percent in February against 3.4 percent in January, the National Statistics Committee said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It gave the following data for Kyrgyz inflation --</p>
<p>    KYRGYZ CONSUMER PRICES     Feb '97     Jan '97     Feb '96</p>
<p>    month-on-month pct change    +2.2	  +3.4	  +3.8</p>
<p>    year-on-year pct change     +33.7	 +34.7	 +28.0</p>
<p>Consumer prices in the first two months of this year grew by 5.6 percent. The goverment targets annual inflation at 20 percent.    --Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
